Description: installers of Legion, in a window and in a terminal
 legion-install-gui, the menu entry "Install Legion", and legion-install, run
 in a terminal with sudo, install Legion from the live session of the USB
 stick on a disk of the computer. They erase the whole disk and divide it
 into an EFI system partition and either one root partition (the default),
 a root partition and /home on a partition of its own, with the sizes you
 choose, or partitions of your own made in an editor: /home, /var, /srv,
 /var/tmp, swap and other folders. All partitions get ext4 or swap and, if
 you choose it, LUKS2 encryption with one passphrase. On a disk with Legion
 and its own /home partition they can instead install Legion again and keep
 /home, /srv and other folders with their files. The installers ask for the
 language, keyboard layout, time zone, disk, partitions, encryption,
 account, computer name and swap, and switch the keyboard of the live
 session to the chosen layout. On an encrypted disk they ask for the disk
 passphrase, show a recovery key and can add a FIDO2 security key.
 .
 The package is meant for the live session only. The installer removes it,
 together with legion-live, from the installed system.

