Description: system settings of Legion
 The apt sources of Debian 13 over HTTPS, the service presets of Legion
 (systemd-networkd and blueman-mechanism off, the UFW firewall and the
 firmware update check on), a udev rule that keeps Bluetooth off the first
 time a computer starts, and a setting that keeps the EFI system partition
 of the live system mounted until shutdown. Each file says in a comment how
 to change it. apt keeps your changes to the files in /etc.
 .
 The system names itself LegionOS. /usr/lib/os-release of this package
 takes the place of the file of base-files through a dpkg diversion (that
 file stays as /usr/lib/os-release.debian), and /etc/issue, /etc/issue.net
 and /etc/motd say LegionOS instead of Debian while they have the text of
 Debian. Removing this package brings the files of Debian back.
 .
 Terminal windows get the LegionOS prompt with the Legion emblem
 (/usr/share/legion-system/prompt.bash, the emblem from legion-artwork). While
 /etc/skel/.bashrc has the text of Debian, the package adds there the lines
 that read the prompt, so accounts made after that have it. Each account
 can remove them from its ~/.bashrc.

